                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm a sucker for voxel graphics.\n\nIt's a multiplayer-only shooter, but doesn't (yet) have a player base. You'll create a profile on first-time login, but can play as any name you want on a per-session basis. The game has three maps with the expected play modes (Capture the Flag, Free-for-All, etc), up to 16 simultaneous. Hosting a match is easy; I don't generally play multiplayer shooters but I figured it immediately without needing to refer to documentation. Framerate was good on an i5 3570 + GTX 1070. Avatar movement felt appropriate and respnsive with expected keymaps. The jet pack is accessed via a double-jump. and propels you in the direction you're facing, so you can turn around mid-leap. It also allows you to access some otherwise inaccessible spots on the map to gain the high ground.\n\nSome of the sounds were missing, such as gun reloads, and some of the English interface text needs another pass by a native speaker, but these are minor issues.\n\nDev, I would approach Bundlestars to get some keys distributed.",
